{"name":"Kauai","hex":"#5ac7ac","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Kauai","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The oldest and fourth-largest island of Hawaii."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Kauai"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kauai (South Africa)","blocks":[{"text":"Kauai is a South African restaurant chain, focused on healthy food options. Founded and headquartered in Cape Town in 1996, it is owned by Real Foods, which itself is owned by Virgin Active South Africa. Kauai operates 200 locations across seven countries around the world."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b7/Kauai_South_Africa_Logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kauai_(South_Africa)","wikidata":"Q136893681"},{"title":"Kauaʻi","blocks":[{"text":"Kauaʻi, sometimes written Kauai, is one of the main Hawaiian Islands. It has an area of 562.3 square miles, making it the fourth largest of the islands and the 21st largest island in the United States. Kauaʻi is 73 mi (117 km) northwest of Oʻahu, across the Kauaʻi Channel. The island's 2020 population was 73,298."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Kauai_from_space_2.jpg/330px-Kauai_from_space_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaua%CA%BBi","wikidata":"Q201026"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Kauai_Store_in_3Arts_Village%2C_Plumstead%2C_Cape_Town.jpg/500px-Kauai_Store_in_3Arts_Village%2C_Plumstead%2C_Cape_Town.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Kauai_Store_in_3Arts_Village%2C_Plumstead%2C_Cape_Town.jpg/1280px-Kauai_Store_in_3Arts_Village%2C_Plumstead%2C_Cape_Town.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https